# qrbin

One Rust package named `qrbin` at the repo root. There is no `qrbin-cli` crate.

- `make` starts in `Makefile` and installs `target/release/qrbin` to `/usr/local/bin/qrbin`. `make build` only compiles. Do not install a second copy under `~/.local/bin`.
- `make deb` and `make linux` start `packaging/build-linux.sh`, then `packaging/Dockerfile`, `packaging/build-inside.sh`, and `packaging/mkdeb.py`.
- Linux output is one glibc 2.27 amd64 build: `dist/qrbin-linux-amd64` and `dist/qrbin_<version>-1_amd64.deb`. It covers Ubuntu 18.04, 22.04, and 24.04.
- Host `cargo` on this Mac is Homebrew. Do not set Cargo's default target away from this machine.
- CLI is `qrbin [OPTIONS] [PAYLOAD]`. Formats are `png` and `svg`. ECC values are `low`, `medium`, `quartile`, and `high`.
- Omit `--theme` for the classic renderer. `--theme` is `plain`, `rounded`, `dots`, or `classy`. Themed output is `qr-code-styling` 0.2.4 with the `png` feature. No `--type`. No 0.1.9.
- No telemetry, HTTP client, update checker, or payload logging.

Before build, install, or packaging work, read `.cursor/skills/qrbin/SKILL.md`.
